.TH "bc_state_set_trap" "3" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server library"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]\(dqbashclient.h\(dq\f[R]

int bc_state_set_trap(bc_client_t *c, const char *signal,
                      const char *command);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets a signal trap on the bash\-server session associated with the
client connection \f[B]c\f[R].
When the specified signal is received (or the specified pseudo\-signal
event occurs), the server session executes the given command string.
.PP
The function sends a \f[CR]set\f[R] request on the STATE channel
(\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R], channel 2) with namespace
\f[CR]\(dqtrap\(dq\f[R], the signal name, and the trap command.
The server performs the equivalent of
\f[CR]trap \(aqcommand\(aq signal\f[R] in the shell session.
.PP
If a trap is already set for the given signal, it is replaced.
